1790667571.126	
1790667571.126	The crucial step toward mechanical reproduction lies in the development of stencils and repeatable matrices. In China, woodblock printing emerged as one of the earliest sophisticated forms of mass image and text dissemination. By carving an entire page or image onto a single wooden plank, scribes could use this block to press ink onto paper repeatedly. This method was incredibly effective for religious texts and popular imagery in East Asia from the Tang Dynasty onward.
1790667571.126	
